<section id="section-10" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>10. Explore Chinatown</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If there&rsquo;s one time I&rsquo;d recommend visiting Bangkok&rsquo;s Chinatown, it&rsquo;s definitely in the evening. The streets look completely different once the neon signs light up, making it a great spot for photography. It&rsquo;s also the perfect place to try some Thai-Chinese street food, with plenty of stalls and small restaurants to choose from. Even if you&rsquo;re not planning to eat much, I&rsquo;d still recommend going for a walk, taking in the atmosphere and enjoying the lively streets after dark.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-11" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>11. Visit a Fairy-Tale Caf&eacute; or a Hidden Garden Restaurant</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If you enjoy discovering cute caf&eacute;s and unique places to eat, Bangkok has some lovely spots that are worth adding to your itinerary. From caf&eacute;s inspired by storybooks to restaurants tucked away in lush gardens, these places offer something a little different from the usual city sightseeing.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={littlePrinceCafe} alt="A latte with a Little Prince design next to a star-shaped cookie at The Little Prince Café in Bangkok" caption="A latte at The Little Prince Café" imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover" />
    <p><strong>The Little Prince Caf&eacute;</strong> &mdash; The Little Prince Caf&eacute; is one of my favorite spots for a quiet coffee break in Bangkok. Inspired by the beloved storybook, it has a charming atmosphere that makes it a lovely place to slow down and enjoy a coffee away from the busy streets. Located in the Sathorn area, it&rsquo;s a great little spot to add to your itinerary if you enjoy cute caf&eacute;s with a unique concept.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={parkSathorn} alt="The garden terrace and bar at Park Sathorn Restaurant in Bangkok" caption="The garden terrace at Park Sathorn Restaurant" imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover" />
    <p><strong>PARK SATHORN RESTAURANT</strong> &mdash; If you&rsquo;re looking for somewhere that feels like a tropical escape in the middle of Bangkok, I&rsquo;d recommend PARK SATHORN RESTAURANT. During my last visit, I loved its lush garden setting, complete with a pond, flowing water, and plenty of greenery. It almost felt like stepping into a hidden tropical oasis, and the food was just as impressive as the surroundings. It&rsquo;s a great option if you want to enjoy a delicious meal somewhere that feels far removed from the city&rsquo;s busy streets.</p>
  </div>
</section>

